## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical PQ migration strategy with backward compatibility, key management, and observability in a production tenant environment.

## Key Concepts

- Post-quantum cryptography integration
- Backward-compatible verification paths (hybrid signatures)
- Per-tenant envelope encryption with versioned keys in a KMS
- JWKS publishing, key rotation, and rollback playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Hybrid JWT verification (conceptual)
function verify(token, publicKeys) {
  if (verifyES256(token, publicKeys.es256)) return true;
  if (verifyPQ(token, publicKeys.pq)) return true;
  return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate no-degradation during rollout?
- What metrics and alerts would trigger a rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical field-level authorization, tenant isolation, and testable guard implementations in GraphQL.

## Key Concepts
- GraphQL authorization at field granularity
- Context-aware tenant checks
- Lightweight middleware/directives for enforcement
- Testing with multi-tenant nested queries

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal field guard in resolver-style form
const resolvers = {
  User: {
    name: (parent, args, ctx) => {
      if (!ctx.user?.permissions?.includes('VIEW_NAME') && ctx.tenantId !== parent.tenantId) {
        throw new Error('Forbidden')
      }
      return parent.name
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this for dynamic permission changes without redeploying?
- What edge cases exist with nested relations and batched resolvers?

